            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0774" n="680" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg680"/>

                <head>No. 424.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Manning to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-11"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 11, 1886</date>.
                        (Received December 20.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 34.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your No. 23, of 2d instant, relative to the loss of certain Government property
                    by troops of the United States, in January last, while engaged in the pursuit of
                    hostile Chiricahua Indians in Mexican territory, and to inclose copy of a note I
                    addressed to Mr. Mariscal, under your instructions, setting forth the case, and
                    asking that the property be returned, or that $2,000, its value and the damages
                    resulting from its loss, be paid to the Government of the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Th. C. Manning.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d424-a1.xml" xpointer="d424-a1"/>
            </div>
